        </div>
        <div class="caption-small">Naturalistic theatre aims to reproduce ordinary life; stylised theatre draws attention to its own artifice. Both are valid — Chekhov's naturalism and Brecht's alienation effect are equally sophisticated responses to the same problem of representation.</div>
      </div>

