    <div class="part-section" id="part-7">

      <h2 class="sec" id="part-h-mythology-gods-heroes-and-the-stories-behind-everything">Part H · mythology — gods, heroes, and the stories behind everything</h2>

      <div class="card u-mb-lg">
        <p class="clabel">Why mythology still matters</p>
        <p class="cval">Myths are not failed science — they are the original technology of meaning</p>
        <p class="cnote">Myths explain origins, encode social values, and give shape to experiences that resist rational account: death, love, war, fate, the cosmos. They were not believed the way facts are believed; they were enacted, re-told, and performed. Greek mythology in particular saturates Western literature, art, and language so thoroughly that you cannot read Homer, Virgil, Dante, Shakespeare, Keats, or Joyce without knowing it. The gods of Olympus are not background decoration; they are the first systematic attempt to map the forces that govern human life.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- Myth origins SVG diagram -->
      <div class="scroll-panel">
        <div class="block-title">Where myths come from — and where they go</div>
        <svg class="literature-media" viewBox="0 0 700 200" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg">
          <defs>
            <marker id="arr-myth" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="6" refX="7" refY="3" orient="auto">
              <polygon points="0 0, 8 3, 0 6" fill="#8A6DB5"/>
            </marker>
          </defs>
          <rect x="10" y="20" width="120" height="44" rx="8" fill="var(--color-background-warning)" stroke="var(--color-border-warning)" stroke-width="0.8"/>
          <text x="70" y="39" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-text-warning)">Natural forces</text>
          <text x="70" y="53" text-anchor="middle" font-size="9" fill="var(--color-text-warning)">thunder, sea, harvest</text>
          <rect x="10" y="78" width="120" height="44" rx="8" fill="var(--color-background-info)" stroke="var(--color-border-info)" stroke-width="0.8"/>
          <text x="70" y="97" text-anchor="middle" font-size="10" font-weight="600" fill="var(--color-text-info)">Social order</text>
