        <div class="muted-text-small">Joseph Campbell's "monomyth" argued that heroic myth follows the same structural pattern globally: departure, initiation, return. Claude Levi-Strauss showed myths resolve cultural contradictions through binary oppositions. Both frameworks have shaped how modern scholars read mythology.</div>
